{
  "_comment": [
    "A batch-insert Decision (`insert_rows`) in the shape the propose path files it:",
    "the target names one database and the body carries every row, each with the id",
    "minted for it at propose time. Three rows, so the card has to render three",
    "tables and two different row titles — a labelled row, a row with no label (the",
    "`Row n` fallback), and a row whose empty cell must not read as a field.",
    "Column keys are Transactions column ids, and `account` / `category` are relation",
    "columns, so their cell values are row ids: the same payload a single-row write",
    "carries, which is the case the read path resolves labels for. Values are neutral",
    "stand-ins for a real proposal; the shape is not."
  ],
